I could not refute the finding. The facts are worse than the reviewer said.

1. The domain does not exist. On 21/10/2026 the .it registry (`whois -h whois.nic.it mypensione.it`) returns «Status: AVAILABLE», and DNS returns NXDOMAIN. So mypensione.it is not just unofficial: anyone can register it. The doc tells users to sign in there «via SPID/CIE», which makes it a ready-made phishing trap.
2. INPS's real services live on inps.it. «La mia pensione futura» has its own page at inps.it/it/it/dettaglio-scheda...la-mia-pensione-futura-simulazione-della-propria-pensione. The contribution statement («Estratto conto contributivo») sits under «Posizione contributiva» (inps.it/it/it/previdenza/posizione-contributiva.html). Access is by SPID, CIE or CNS. The INPS PIN for citizens was dropped in 2021, so the «PIN/CIE/SPID» at previdenza-obbligatoria.md:225 is also out of date.
